# Copy to .dev.vars (gitignored) for `wrangler dev`. Production values are set with
# `wrangler secret put <NAME> --env faithnet` and never live in wrangler.toml.

# HMAC-SHA256 key for the session tokens BOTH sign-in paths mint (POST /dev/session and POST
# /auth/home). Without it `wrangler dev` falls back to a fixed insecure dev secret; a deployment must
# set it (`wrangler secret put SESSION_SECRET --env faithnet`).
SESSION_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-random-string

# Home sign-in needs no secret: the OIDC client `pokernight` is public and PKCE-bound, and its
# client_id / delegate / redirect_uri are vars in wrangler.toml. Note the ONLY registered redirect_uri
# is https://poker.faithnet.io/, so the real ceremony cannot complete against www.faithnet.me from
# localhost — local dev uses POST /dev/session.

# chain-rpc-gateway app token for the tables Worker (phase 3, mandate-transfer settlement). Unused in phase 1.
RPC_TOKEN=

# Private key of the EOA that custodies the house Smart Agents (HOUSE_SERVICE_SA and
# HOUSE_TREASURY_SA in wrangler.toml). It only ever SIGNS the userOpHash of a house transfer —
# `AgentAccount.execute` is gated to the EntryPoint, so this key cannot move the asset by itself and
# never holds it. Provision it with `pnpm provision:house`, which writes it (and nothing else) to
# .house-key.json at the repo root (gitignored, mode 0600); copy the `privateKey` field here for
# local dev, and for a deployment set it as a SECRET, never a var:
#
#   pnpm --filter pokernight-tables exec wrangler secret put HOUSE_CUSTODIAN_KEY --env faithnet
#
# Rotating it means re-running provisioning with a new key: the Smart Agent addresses are derived
# from the custodian, so a new key is a new pair of accounts.
HOUSE_CUSTODIAN_KEY=

# Operator authority for `DELETE /tables/:id/seat/:seat`, the one route that can take a seat away from
# a player who did not ask to leave. Presented in its OWN header:
#
#   curl -X DELETE -H "x-operator-token: $OPERATOR_TOKEN" \
#        https://tables.faithnet.io/tables/<tableId>/seat/<seat>
#
# A separate header from `Authorization: Bearer` on purpose: an operator token must never be
# mistakeable for a player session, and no session can ever be promoted into one — there is no admin
# ROLE in this app, and this secret is the whole of the authority. It is compared in CONSTANT TIME
# (src/operator.ts digests both sides first, so neither the value nor its length leaks through
# timing), it is never logged and never appears in a response body.
#
# Holding it is not enough to clear a seat. Three further conditions about the SEAT must also hold:
# no live socket, not in a running hand, and idle beyond SEAT_IDLE_MS. Every refusal names which one
# failed. Leave this UNSET and no seat can be cleared by anyone, which is the right default.
#
#   pnpm --filter pokernight-tables exec wrangler secret put OPERATOR_TOKEN --env faithnet
OPERATOR_TOKEN=
